<title>USA: Blue-chip stocks end lower.</title>
<headline>Blue-chip stocks end lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blue-chip stocks closed weaker Thursday after a rollercoaster session as an unexpectedly weak August durable goods report left traders scrambling to sell some economically sensitive issues.</p>
<p>Based on early and unofficial data, the Dow Jones industrial average ended down 8.51 points at 5,868.85.</p>
<p>In the broader market, advancing issues led declines 13-9 on active volume of about 500 million shares on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
